  33:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** \n
  34:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  35:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** The fsReg package provides the parts outlined in the model. By compilation switch, the Reg task may
  36:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** the usual operating mode or in test harness mode. When running in the usual operating mode, the tes
  37:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** will not be linked to the package. When running in test harness mode, stub services are provided, s
  38:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** Register checking interface is separated from being called and only the test server will be able to
  39:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** \n
  40:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  41:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** Checking the program counter register and the stack pointer register at normal operational work is 
  42:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** as these registers get checked during program execution and calling functions and passing parameter
  43:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** checking work registers depends on the type of controller, so the real task is implemented using as
  44:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** This high level language part is only meant to be a portable wrapper function on its top. So, its i
  45:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** mind that names of entry points can't be changed freely, except they get normalized for all types o
  46:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** \n
  47:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** \n
  48:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsReg.c **** \n
